---
kind: lore
id: lamplight.casebook
title: Inspector Wren's casebook
series: casebook
---

<entry id="pageWatch" on="review" category="casebook" title="The watch" when="holds('found', ['watch'])">
  @inspector{code="0010"}: Hask's watch, stopped at 1:15, crystal cracked. Solt calls the time of death from it.
</entry>

<entry id="pageDoor" on="review" category="casebook" title="The singer at the door" when="holds('placed', ['lise'])">
  @inspector{code="0010"}: Lise Varo was at compartment 7 at 1:15 — the minute the watch stopped. She handed him an envelope. The porter swears to the time.
</entry>

<entry id="pageCufflink" on="review" category="casebook" title="M. D." when="holds('found', ['cufflink'])">
  @inspector{code="0010"}: Gold cufflink under the berth, engraved M. D. Mirela Dace says she has not seen her uncle in three years.
  <match subject="entry.mirelaCufflink.everRead">
    <when is="true">
      @inspector{code="0020"}: Her father's. Hask took them as interest and wore them to spite her. A cufflink that falls off the victim's own wrist is not a clue.
    </when>
    <otherwise>
      @inspector{code="0030"}: Ask her.
    </otherwise>
  </match>
</entry>

<entry id="pageTime" on="review" category="casebook" title="The hour" when="@timeFixed">
  @inspector{code="0010"}: Alive at 1:55 — Crane brought his tea. Dead by 2:10 — no answer to the lamp knock. He died in the Orla tunnel, in the four minutes of dark.
</entry>

<entry id="pageWatchLies" on="review" category="casebook" title="The watch lies" when="holds('falseClue', ['watch'])">
  @inspector{code="0010"}: The watch says 1:15 and the man was alive at 1:55. Somebody set it. Somebody wanted the hour to be 1:15.
</entry>

<entry id="pageAlibis" on="review" category="casebook" title="Who was where" when="count('alibi', ['_', 'tunnel']) >= 3">
  @inspector{code="0010"}: In the tunnel: Crane in the van with the porter. Dace and Varo in the dining car, each vouching for the other. Three of four.
</entry>

<entry id="pageCrane" on="review" category="casebook" title="The man with the passkey" when="holds('opportunity', ['crane'])">
  @inspector{code="0010"}: Crane has keys to every door on the train and nobody has yet put him anywhere during the tunnel.
  @inspector{code="0020"}: Nobody can yet place {{@unaccounted:plural(one suspect|# suspects)}} away from compartment 7 in the tunnel.
</entry>

<entry id="pageOneLeft" on="review" category="casebook" title="One left" when="count('opportunity', ['_']) == 1">
  @inspector{code="0010"}: Of the four, only one cannot be put anywhere during the tunnel by somebody else's eyes.
</entry>

<entry id="pageShape" on="review" category="casebook" title="A shape in the corridor" when="holds('seen', ['solt', 'corridor', 'tunnel'])">
  @inspector{code="0010"}: In the dark of the Orla, by the light of one match, a tall man with spectacles passed the dining-car door, going toward the sleepers. Solt's berth was empty. Solt says he was asleep.
</entry>

<entry id="pageSoltLied" on="review" category="casebook" title="The empty berth" when="holds('lied', ['solt'])">
  @inspector{code="0010"}: Solt says he slept in five through the tunnel. Crane found five empty at 2:10, bed made. The doctor was out of his berth in the dark and lied about it.
</entry>

<entry id="pageBerths" on="review" category="casebook" title="Empty berths" when="@emptyBerths >= 1">
  @inspector{code="0010"}: Beds made and empty in the Orla: {{@emptyBerths:plural(one|#)}}.
</entry>

<entry id="pageSolt" on="review" category="casebook" title="Motive, means, the chance" when="holds('prime', ['solt'])">
  @inspector{code="0010"}: Four hundred crowns or the Medical Board. A bottle of laudanum a third gone. No one on this train can put him anywhere in the tunnel but where he says he was, and where he says he was is empty.
  @inspector{code="0020"}: Emmerich Solt.
</entry>
